{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Data Abstraction", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 2, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 1, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.1", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about abstract data types.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Describe common activities at work to a visitor using short sentences in familiar spoken and written situations.  Understand information about data and its structure in simple spoken and written situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations.   Describes common activities related to Software Programming through the use of appropriate expressions, grammar and vocabulary in written or spoken situations according to the abilities related to this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "enpe7n3le01ob02re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Infinitives of Purpose to Start a Sentence", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "We use infinitives to express the purpose of an action.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "To have a complete abstract stack data type, it has to include a structure for sorting data, as a list, an array, or a queue, and a set of operations such as adding or removing integers from the stack.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "To understand data types, we need to identify its advantages.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "To access the data contained in an object, we must have the functions (the class) of the abstract data type.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<p>The <strong>infinitive</strong> is always used to express the goal or purpose of one or more actions. You use the <strong>infinitive</strong> to start a sentence, by following this structure:</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>To </strong>+ base form of the verb.</p> <p>Example: <strong><i>To develop </i></strong><i>a computer game, I need to work hard.</i></p> <p>Remember that in this case, you can use the infinitive as the subject of the sentence.</p> <p>For example: <strong><i>To design</i></strong><i> a software, I need to know all the requirements.</i></p> <p>However, you can also use infinitives as the complement of a sentence or as the object of the sentence</p> <p>For example:<i> </br>I need to know all the requirements <strong>to design</strong> a software.</i> (Complement of a sentence)</br><i> I need <strong>to know</strong> all the requirements to design a software.</i> (Infinitive as the object of a sentence)</p>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Infinitives of Purpose\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Purpose\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Actions \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i><span class=\\\"strong\\\">To</span> analyze data,\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i>we need to know the context\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i><span class=\\\"strong\\\">To</span> interpret the context\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i>the engineer has to know the programming language.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Countable and Uncountable Nouns Related to Software Programming and Data", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "There are nouns in software programing which are countable or uncountable. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "It has to include a structure for sorting data, as a list, an array, or a queue.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The data class is like the encapsulation of an object.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<p><strong><i>Countable</i></strong> nouns are things or people we can number as a single unit and/or as plurals.</p>  <p>Examples:</br> <i>A record- Record<strong>s</strong>.</i></br> <i>A structure- Structure<strong>s</strong>.</i></p>  <p>Remember that when you have more than one item, you use the plural form of the noun; plurals are usually made by adding an &ldquo;<strong>s</strong>&rdquo; to the singular form of the noun.</p>  <p>Examples:</br> <i>Operation- operation<strong>s</strong></i></br> Representation- representation<strong>s</strong></p>  <p>Be careful! Not all the plurals are form by adding an &ldquo;<strong>s</strong>&rdquo; or &ldquo;<strong>es</strong>&rdquo;, there some irregular plurals.</p>  <p>Let's see some examples:&nbsp;<br /> <strong>Singular - Plural</strong><br />Medium - Media&nbsp;<br />Phenomenon - Phenomena<br />Data - Datum&nbsp;</p>  <p><strong><i>Uncountable</i></strong> nouns are things we cannot conceive as units, we cannot number them.</p>  <p>Le't see some examples:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":1,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Nouns in Software Programming\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Countable\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Uncountable\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Representations.<br/> \\tQueue.<br/> Records.<br/> DAQs.<br/> Codes.<br/> Data.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Software.<br/> Acquisition.<br/> Abstraction.<